.TH QLOGIN 1 "2026-11-08" "qlogin" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qlogin \- quick terminal login greeter (PAM)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qlogin
[\fB\-t\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Asks for a user name and a password on the terminal it runs on, authenticates through the PAM service
.IR qlogin ,
lets the user pick a session, registers it with
.BR qlogind (8)
(or any org.freedesktop.login1 service) through CreateSession, exports XDG_SESSION_ID, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, XDG_SEAT, XDG_VTNR and XDG_SESSION_TYPE,
writes utmp, wtmp and lastlog, and executes the session. It exits when the session ends; init is expected to start it again.
.PP
The password is typed without any echo into one mlock(2)ed page, wiped as soon as pam_authenticate returns. Failed logins wait 1, 2, 4, ... up to 30 seconds;
keys typed during the wait are discarded. Ctrl-C returns to the user name prompt. Ctrl-D on an empty user name exits.
.PP
Sessions come from /usr/share/wayland-sessions, /usr/share/xsessions, ~/.config/qlogin/*.desktop, and always the login shell.
The last choice is stored in ~/.config/qlogin/last.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
Show the microseconds from main() to the first prompt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PAM_CONFIG
Test mode: PAM reads $PAM_CONFIG/qlogin. Also disables setuid, tty chown, and contact with the system bus unless DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS is set. Tests only.
.TP
.B QLOGIN_VAR, QLOGIN_SESSDIRS, QLOGIN_DELAY_UNIT_MS, QLOGIN_HOME
Test mode only: fake var tree, session directories, lockout unit, home directory.
.SH FILES
/etc/pam.d/qlogin (not installed by this project)
.SH BUGS
Not tried on a real system as a login service. X11 sessions are launched with startx and are untested. See readme.md for the full list.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qlogind (8)
